# OUTCOME REVIEW, 2026-09-28 (window: cycles 112–116)

**Verdict on the claim: refuted.** Five cycles, about 647 minutes and at least $146, produced five more intermediate files that cannot run. The one VI that beat the original, accepted the day before, was not touched, described, or offered to the user.

Limits of this review:
- `claudeDev\` is outside the repository, so I could not check any VI file; md5s and sizes are as the logs state them.
- Cycle 116 has no recorded cost (`tools/bench/cycle_runner.log:748`, `$?`), so the dollar total is a floor.
- I used no external sources.

## 1. DELIVERABLE

Nothing. The user can run today exactly what they could run at the last review.

| File saved this window | Cycle | State | Source |
|---|---|---|---|
| `D1_l2_b2a_20260928_001426.vi` | 112 | intermediate bed | `STATUS.md:180` |
| `D1_l2_b2b_20260928_015450.vi` | 113 | intermediate bed | `STATUS.md:155` |
| `D1_l2_b3_20260928_032703.vi` | 114 | intermediate bed | `STATUS.md:132-134` |
| `D1_l2_r1_20260928_055441.vi` | 115 | "STRUCTURAL, ExecState 0 by design, never run" | `STATUS.md:64` |
| none | 116 | "no new file" | `STATUS.md:76` |

- The evidence for these files is Error List item counts (83, 65, 59, 55) and graph diffs. None of it is a run.
- No benchmark row was added: INDEX still ends at row 59, dated 2026-09-27 (`archive/benchmarks/INDEX.md:80`), and the counted output shows 59 at both reviews.
- The only runnable product remains `D1_s1_disp_20260927_041648.vi` from cycle 110 (`STATUS.md:18`), unchanged.
- The counted output still names `Track_v6_CPU_core_v0.vi` and `Track_v6_CPU_queue_v0.vi` as the deliverables. A glob finds neither in the repository, and the line omits the display-loop VI. The last review reported the same thing.

